s strong teamwork and cooperative behavior that outweighs their minor flaws, I would reconsider.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}", "thoughts": "We have info from agent_2: no extra D attributes.\n\nNow as agent_1, we need to produce our public message. We have our own knowledge: list of attributes for each candidate. Summarize evaluation.\n\nWe need to consider strengths and weaknesses for long-distance pilot.\n\nLet's list:\n\nCandidate A:\nStrengths: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities.\nWeaknesses: sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized.\n\nCandidate B:\nStrengths: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills.\nWeaknesses: can be grumpy, can be uncooperative.\n\nCandidate C:\nStrengths: can make correct decisions quickly, known to be 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew.\nWeaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further education.\n\nCandidate D:\nStrengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously.\nWeaknesses: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe need to weigh for long-distance flights: reliability, technical competence, calm under pressure, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nAssess each:\n\nA: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership - good for navigation, situational awareness. Weaknesses: criticism, unorganized could affect paperwork, crew relations.\n\nB: conscientious, stress handling, weather assessment, computer skills - good for planning, tech. Weaknesses: grumpy, uncooperative could affect crew.\n\nC: quick correct decisions, 100% reliable, positive crew atmosphere - strong reliability, crew. Weaknesses: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (long-term development). Might affect teamwork and learning.\n\nD: problem solving, concentration, responsibility, handles unexpected events - good for emergencies. Weaknesses: arrogant, weak leadership - could affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to pick best overall. Likely Candidate C seems strong reliability, decision-making, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be problematic for teamwork. Candidate B has good stress handling and weather, but uncooperative. Candidate A has strong anticipation and leadership but unorganized. Candidate D strong problem solving but weak leadership.\n\nWhich is best? For long-distance, reliability and decision-making under pressure are crucial, plus teamwork. C is 100% reliable, quick decisions, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty could hinder. However positive atmosphere may offset some communication issues. Egocentric could be a risk. Not willing to further education may affect long-term.\n\nB's stress handling and weather assessment are important for long flights. But uncooperative could be serious.\n\nA's anticipation and spatial vision are valuable for navigation, but unorganized could be safety risk.\n\nD's problem solving and concentration are good, but weak leadership and arrogance could degrade crew.\n\nOverall, I think Candidate C is strongest overall due to reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere, despite communication issues. The tradeoff is communication difficulty and lack of willingness to develop further. If we could get evidence about communication ability, that could change.\n\nThus provisional preference: Candidate C, confidence moderate (maybe 65%). Uncertainty: communication and egocentric traits.\n\nWe need to mention evidence from others: we have only agent_2's response about D lacking extra info. No other contributions.\n\nNow produce output."}
